Sval: a refused agent load shows about:agentblocked

Sval's agent gate cancels a top-level load the user blocked for the agent
whose tab it is, and one whose tab could not be given its owner first.
Cancelled with NS_ERROR_ABORT the tab shows nothing, and with
NS_ERROR_BLOCKED_BY_POLICY it shows Firefox's "Your organization has
blocked" page, which is not what happened. Two error codes of their own map
in nsDocShell::DisplayLoadError to a page of Sval's, which says which
refusal it was. A front end cannot choose the error page a cancelled load
shows, so this needs the docshell.

diff --git a/browser/components/about/AboutRedirector.cpp b/browser/components/about/AboutRedirector.cpp
